      "writtenOn": "2017-08-07T20:55:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Looks like the limit of file descriptors on our machines is 32768, but I think the linux default is 1024 or 4096, and our mac machines default to 256!  So I guess you _can_ run out of threads, but if you are running out of threads you will definitely run out of file descriptors at much lower values on some machines.",
      "parentUuid": "9de45e6c_99607b24",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 557,
