    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "eb853eae_e1a134b8",
        "filename": "finder/finder.go",
        "patchSetId": 15
      },
      "lineNbr": 560,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002751
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-08-07T18:28:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This WaitGroup seems dangerous, WaitGroup has a strict requirement that calling Add when the counter is at 0 must not happen concurrently with any calls to Wait, which is hard to guarantee when you reuse the threadpool for a bunch of different APIs.  I think the WaitGroup should stay in the function that uses it.",
      "revId": "e5dfc55850765f161da4053334fbafb0d8d3ccef",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "402be003_94aa6d40",
        "filename": "finder/finder.go",
        "patchSetId": 15
      },
      "lineNbr": 560,
      "author": {
        "id": 1137668
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-08-07T20:46:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yeah I was able to do that in one case in startFromExternalCache on line 852. I assume the case on line 182 is the one you\u0027re talking about.\n\nEven if the WaitGroup didn\u0027t have that requirement (that calling Wait() could potentially crash while the counter was 0 and another caller was calling Add()), that pattern of usage would still be a race condition anyway and could risk inconsistent behavior. Consequently, every caller that calls Add() either is called before Wait(), or is called while the counter is known to be positive.\n\nIt would be possible to make startFromExternalCache block until all of its calls complete, which would facilitate making its ThreadPool into a local variable. That seems inconvenient though.\n\nHow about I modify the ThreadPool such that after the completion of any Wait, any subsequent call to Run will fail (to enforce the inability to reuse its WaitGroup)?",
      "parentUuid": "eb853eae_e1a134b8",
      "revId": "e5dfc55850765f161da4053334fbafb0d8d3ccef",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
